  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't build or run it, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. The soldier model is loaded from /assets/soldier.glb and plays `Walk` on a loop. It moves counter-clockwise on a radius-4 circle around the origin, with its yaw set from the direction of travel. Pressing `r` crossfades to `Run` over 0.4 s and eases the speed up from 1.4 to 3.6 m/s. Pressing `w` goes back to `Walk` the same way. The scene has a ground plane, a shadow-casting directional light, a fill light, a hemisphere light, a neutral environment and a fixed perspective camera that frames the whole circle. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nTwo things are unchecked:\n- **Facing direction:** I assumed the model faces +Z at zero yaw. If it walks backwards, flip the yaw sign in `place()`.\n- **Model hash:** I reused the sha256 from the docs recipe (`dfb230fc…`) for `soldier.glb` without comparing it to the file. If the hash check rejects the model, that value is the one to fix.",
